Package: rnaparallel
Type: Package
Title: Parallel Companions for RNA-Seq Tools
Version: 0.4.9
Authors@R: c(
    person("GenomeRx", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "author of the parallel companion"),
    person("Nam", "Nguyen", email = "namnguyenhk@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Yuqing", "Zhang", role = "ctb",
           comment = "author of ComBat-seq, accelerated but not modified by this package"),
    person("Giovanni", "Parmigiani", role = "ctb", comment = "author of ComBat-seq"),
    person("W. Evan", "Johnson", role = "ctb", comment = "author of ComBat-seq"))
Description: Parallel companions for RNA-seq tools. A companion never
    reimplements the method: it calls the original function with its hot paths
    rebound to row-parallel versions in a child of that function's own
    environment, so every other symbol still resolves to the original code and
    the result is identical() to a serial run rather than merely close to it.
    ComBat-seq is the first. Its per-gene quantile matching, edgeR GLM fits and
    tagwise dispersion estimation are split by gene row, and the common
    dispersion is dispatched across batches. Works against Bioconductor sva or a
    sourced copy of the upstream zhangyuqing/ComBat-seq repository, whichever is
    loaded, and dispatches its parallelism through mclapply, future,
    BiocParallel, foreach or serial. Companions for limma lmFit and
    duplicateCorrelation, and for edgeR normLibSizes, follow the same
    construction. The established calcNormFactors_parallel name remains the
    public compatibility API.
